      "statement": "The J5 auto-approve: recordAutoApproveShadow (AUTONOMY_SHADOW_ENABLED) records one auto_approve_shadow judgment per approval under a conservative rule (test-only, not high-risk/security, >= 3 verified outcomes and no regression in class, model rule-v1); when the rule says yes and testGapAutoApproveScope returns a single new test file under packages/server/src/__tests__ (LOOP_AUTO_APPROVE_TEST_GAP; M2 mutation-gap lane additionally requires LOOP_AUTO_APPROVE_MUTATION_GAP and >= 1 verified lane run), the daemon pins auto_approved_scope on the lease and decides via decideWorkerApproval with decidedBy autonomy:test-gap-rule-v1; with ORACLE_LANES_AUTO_APPROVE=true an oracle-lane maker is approved on the same one-file scope even when rule-v1 says no (decidedBy autonomy:oracle-lane-v1, Z4, the rule verdict still recorded); the auto_approved_scope verification gate fails the run if the maker changed anything but that file.",
